<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ridda Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/632">632</a>–<a href="/years/633">633 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ridda Wars, or Wars of Apostasy, were a series of campaigns fought in 632–633 CE by the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>, Abu Bakr, against Arabian tribes that broke away after the death of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophet-muhammad">Prophet Muhammad</a>. Many tribes rallied around rival prophetic claimants such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musaylima">Musaylima</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sajah">Sajah</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a> describe how Abu Bakr divided his forces into eleven corps and reunified <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, preparing the ground for the great conquests.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ridda-wars.jpg" alt="Ridda Wars" width="320" height="271" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mohammad Adil / Mohammad adil at en.wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mohammad_adil-Riddah_wars.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
